.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt UMASK 1
.Os Project9
.Sh NAME
.Nm umask
.Nd display or change the file creation mask
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar octal-mask
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a shell built-in.
With no argument it prints the current mask.
With an argument it sets the mask to an octal value between 000 and 777.
The mask clears bits from mode 0666 for files and 0777 for directories.
Children inherit the mask.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Set a mask for private files and directories.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
umask 077
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chmod 1
